s.jpg/330px-Chardin_-_Les_attributs_des_arts.jpg",0,35,1,0],[138412969,"Q138412969",null,36,null,null,2,"4/46/Chardin_-_Wildenstein_1969%2C_105.png/330px-Chardin_-_Wildenstein_1969%2C_105.png",1,35,1,0],[138851100,"Head of a statue of Psamtik II",-592,null,null,null,3,"a/ad/T%C3%AAte_d%27une_statue_de_Psamm%C3%A9tique_II%2C_mus%C3%A9e_Jacquemart_Andr%C3%A9.jpg/330px-T%C3%AAte_d%27une_statue_de_Psamm%C3%A9tique_II%2C_mus%C3%A9e_Jacquemart_Andr%C3%A9.jpg",3,36,1,0]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaries":{"651579":["The Putti candle-holders are a pair of c.1434-1439 sculptures by Donatello, now in the Musée Jacquemart-André in Paris.","Putti candle-holders"],"762552":["The Hours of Jean de Boucicaut is believed to have been created between 1405 and 1408. It contains the Paris Liturgy of the Hours.","Hours of Jean de Boucicaut"],"1239065":["Ecce Homo is a painting by the Renaissance painter Andrea Mantegna. It is conserved at Musée Jacquemart-André in Paris.","Ecce Homo (Mantegna)"],"3232204":["The New Model is a c. 1770 oil-on-canvas painting by Jean-Honoré Fragonard, acquired by Édouard André before his marriage and now in the Musée Jacquemart-André.","The New Model"],"3399490":["Portrait of comte Antoine Français de Nantes is an 1811 oil on wood panel painting by Jacques-Louis David, showing Antoine Français de Nantes, prefect, comte d'Empire and grand officier of the Légion d’honneur.","Portrait of comte Antoine Français de Nantes"],"3842434":["The Madonna and Child with Three Saints is a 1490-1500 tempera on canvas painting attributed to Andrea Mantegna, now in the Musée Jacquemart-André in Paris. Heavily damaged, not all art historians attribute it as an autograph work.","Madonna and Child with Three Saints (Mantegna)"],"3842511":["Madonna and Child with Saint Jerome and Saint Louis of Toulouse is a c.1455 tempera on panel painting by Andrea Mantegna.","Madonna and Child with Saint Jerome and Saint Louis of Toulouse"],"5968478":["Henry III Received at the Villa Contarini or Henry III's Visit to the Villa Contarini is a 1750 fresco by Giovanni Battista Tiepolo, now in the Musée Jacquemart-André in Paris. It shows Henry III of France visiting the Italian Contarini family in 1574.","Henry III Received at the Villa Contarini"],"16038645":["Portrait of Mathilde de Canisy, Marquise d'Antin is a 1738 oil-on-canvas portrait by Jean-Marc Nattier, produced ten years before he became official painter to the French royal family. It is now in the Musée Jacquemart-André, in Paris.","Portrait of Mathilde de Canisy, Marquise d'Antin"],"16038699":["Portrait of a Man is a c.1660 oil-on-canvas portrait of an unknown subject by the Dutch artist Frans Hals, produced late in his career. Acquired by Édouard André, it is now in the Musée Jacquemart-André in Paris.","Portrait of a Man (Frans Hals, Musée Jacquemart-André)"],"21401882":["Supper at Emmaus or The Pilgrims at Emmaus is a c.1628 oil on panel painting by Rembrandt, now in the Musée Jacquemart-André in Paris","Supper at Emmaus (Rembrandt, Musée Jacquemart-André)"],"41433015":["Portrait of Countess Catherine Skavronskaya is a 1790 oil-on-canvas portrait by Elisabeth Vigée-Lebrun, now in the Musée Jacquemart-André in Paris.","Portrait of Countess Yekaterina Skavronskaya"]}}